2d/xsp_wiener.en:
``a`` sweeps the neighbourhood window size over the odd values 3, 5, 7, 9 (``k = 3 + 2*int(a*3)``;
a=0 gives 3, a close to 1 gives 9). ``b`` is unused. An adaptive filter that automatically estimates the noise variance
from the local variance; unlike the Gaussian/mean box, which even out with uniform strength,
it evens out flat regions more strongly, while regions of large variance (with many edges/textures)
tend to be preserved. Since it assumes Gaussian noise, it is unsuitable for salt-and-pepper noise.
The output is clipped to [0,1].

2d/xkor_gaussian.en:
a sweeps sigma over the range 0.3–3.0 (``0.3 + 2.7 * a``). b is unused.
On the CPU it is not faster than the scipy version (an implementation that pays off on GPU / batch execution;
with ``IMGEVOLVE_KORNIA_DEVICE=cuda`` it runs on the GPU).

